messages:
sara (Support): Customer acme-product reports that streaming responses stop after ~1s when using node edge SDK on Vercel. They see the ReadableStream close early after our auth token rotates.

ben (Support): Which SDK version? Any repro? :thinking:

sara (Support): Using @redwood/sdk-node v0.11.2 (edge build). Repro attached below. Happens consistently when token TTL < response time (~5s). Logs: ```
[2026-02-15T11:02:01Z] fetch /v1/streams 200
[2026-02-15T11:02:03Z] token rotated -> new jwt
[2026-02-15T11:02:03Z] client stream closed by runtime
```

mike (Eng:runtime): This sounds like the edge runtime aborting the underlying fetch when the Authorization header changes. Can you paste minimal repro (edge) code?

sara (Support): Repro (Vercel Edge function):
```js
export default async function handler(req) {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/streams', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.RW_TOKEN}` },
    body: JSON.stringify({ model: 'redwood-small', input: 'hello' }),
  });
  const reader = res.body.getReader();
  while (true) {
    const { done, value } = await reader.read();
    if (done) break;
    // simulate slow processing
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1500));
    console.log(new TextDecoder().decode(value));
  }
  return new Response('ok');
}
```

anjali (DevEx): Interesting — token rotation is done by our auth middleware which can mutate headers on the fly. In edge, changing req/connection headers can trigger stream aborts. Two quick asks: (1) can customer run without rotation (long-lived token) to confirm? (2) can they try SDK v0.12.0-beta which changed how we attach auth for streaming?

ben (Support): Customer tried long-lived token -> stream stays open. They can't use long TTL in prod. Asked for workaround.

mike (Eng:runtime): Short-term workaround: avoid re-attaching Authorization mid-stream. Instead, send a pre-signed per-request ephemeral header or put token in query param (signed) so the fetch's initial headers never mutate. Longer-term, we should ensure SDK sets Authorization once and doesn't update headers while streaming on edge runtimes. I'll open a fix.

deploy-bot: Deployment queued: patch/edge-auth-stream-guard -> staging

anjali (DevEx): I'll prepare a short note for support with repro steps and suggested mitigations (use v0.12.0-beta or pre-signed query param). Also add a snippet showing how to use a per-request ephemeral token.

sara (Support): Shared guidance with customer and asked to try v0.12.0-beta. If they see continued closures, escalate to eng-runtime with full trace logs.

mike (Eng:runtime): Filed RW-9342 with reproducer and logs. Root cause: header mutation triggers the V8 Fetch abort signal in edge. Planned fix: keep headers immutable for streaming responses and decouple auth refresh.

ben (Support): Marking as customer-blocker until patch lands. Thanks all :thumbsup:
